  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Fr&#xe4;mja inkludering i Jerusalem</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Promoting inclusiveness in Jerusalem</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Core support to  a non-governmental organisation with the purpose to monitor and analyse the geo-political situation in Jerusalem. Terrestrial Jerusalem&apos;s focus is to influence Jerusalem-centric policy with three goals in mind: 1) to prevent harmful developments that could ignite crises and derail prospects for a political solution, 2) to promote constructive, affordable and achievable interventions that can stabilise the situation and 3) to develop medium and long-term strategies that will contribute to a sustainable two-state solution.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">K&#xe4;rnst&#xf6;d till en civilsamh&#xe4;llesorganisation med syfte att f&#xf6;lja och analysera den geopolitiska situationen i Jerusalem. Terrestrial Jerusalem avser att influera Jerusalem-centrisk policy med tre huvudm&#xe5;ls&#xe4;ttningar: 1) att motverka skadlig utveckling som skulle kunna generera kriser och om&#xf6;jligg&#xf6;ra en framtida tv&#xe5;statsl&#xf6;sning; 2) fr&#xe4;mja konstruktiva, kostnadseffektiva och m&#xf6;jliga &#xe5;tg&#xe4;rder som kan stabilisera situationen; och 3) utveckla strategier som kan bidra till en h&#xe5;llbar tv&#xe5;statsl&#xf6;sning.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The overarching objective of Terrestrial Jerusalem&apos;s activities is to: protect the political, religious, territorial and cultural character of Jerusalem; to promote a just, equitable and sustainable political settlement to the Israeli-Palestinian conflict that respect the rights of all its residents; and to safeguard prospects for realizing a two-state solution.</narrative>
  </description>
